            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "I checked from update service side and you have brought in required changes into common task generation logic, except few comments. \n\nPending UT."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/task_generation.hpp",
                    "line": 40,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "I think this should also add an error message into taskData, isn't it?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/task_generation.hpp",
                    "line": 40,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "I intentionally didn't do that because failure to parse one message shouldn't really fail the task.  At most we could log InternalError, which isn't really that helpful to a user watching the task.  At least that was my thinking.\n\nIs there a use case where logging this to the task would be important?  The only way I think it can happen is if a service publishes a bad dbus interface."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/task_generation.hpp",
                    "line": 40,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "> I intentionally didn't do that because failure to parse one message shouldn't really fail the task.  At most we could log InternalError, which isn't really that helpful to a user watching the task.  At least that was my thinking.\n> \n> Is there a use case where logging this to the task would be important?  The only way I think it can happen is if a service publishes a bad dbus interface.\n\nYes, thats what i think it would catch - a non-existent (but required) DBus interface."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/task_generation.hpp",
                    "line": 40,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
